# SQL-Ledger keeps site configuration, login data and per-dataset runtime
# state inside the source tree. None of it belongs in a public repository.

# ------------------------------------------------------- site configuration
# Created at install time by copying sql-ledger.conf.default; holds the
# database connection settings for this install.
/sql-ledger.conf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- login data
# users/members holds the login sections including crypt'ed passwords and the
# uuencoded database password; users/*.conf are the per-login %myconfig
# snippets. sql-ledger.eps and sql-ledger.png are distributed files and stay.
users/members*
users/*.conf
users/*.LCK

# ------------------------------------------- per-dataset runtime directories
# admin.pl creates one of each when a dataset is created. templates/ and
# spool/ ship empty and git cannot track empty directories -- recreate them
# after cloning:
#   mkdir -p templates spool && chown apache:apache templates spool
/templates/*/
/spool/*
/images/*/
